So assert: (item == null) => this.lastElement() == null && (item != null) => this.lastElement().equals(item) ? But equality for objects: use == for null, .equals for non-null. Usually spec uses == for reference equality? In previous examples they used .equals for objects. Eg earlier they used this.query(i).equals(\old(this.query(i))). So we can use .equals. For null we need to check this.lastElement() == null.

