But precedence: && lower than =>? Actually => lower priority than && and ||, meaning && binds tighter. So expression A => B && C => D is parsed as (A => (B && (C => D))) which is not intended. So need parentheses around each implication and combine with &&. So:

assert (item == null) => (this.lastElement() == null) && (item != null) => this.lastElement().equals(item);

